<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at 52 µm for the Late Pleistocene marine stickleback (Pass 2 specimen-locked) (Gasterosteus aculeatus_marine)",
        "Schnakenberg wavelength at 52 µm for the Late Pleistocene marine stickleback (Pass 2 specimen-locked) faithfully reproduces Gasterosteus aculeatus_marine morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gasterosteus aculeatus_marine specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Gasterosteus aculeatus_marine" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That 52 µm was measured on a fossil melanophore",
        "does_not_claim: That N_eff = 8 is a published plate count for G. doryssus_late",
        "does_not_claim: That the specimen-locked frame is an independent prediction rather than a fit on one photograph",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Gain 0.0316 chosen as the largest trial with radial Pearson above 0.98 and CV at least 70",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters placed so the marine wavelength is 52 µm",
        "reconstructed_in_script: λ(N) = 52 µm * sqrt(32/N) for doryssus_late (104 µm) and living aculeatus (78 µm)",
        "reported_in_source: Bell, Baumgartner and Olson (1985) temporal change in G. doryssus armor characters",
        "reported_in_source: Colosimo et al. (2004, 2005) Eda complete-plate versus low-plate morphs",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) critical wavenumber from the dispersion determinant",
        "transfer_boundary: A small gain preserves the photograph's spectrum; it does not prove melanophores were measured at 52 µm",
        "transfer_boundary: N_eff = 8 for the predecessor is the Colosimo low-morph analogy, not a Truckee plate count",
        "transfer_boundary: The 2020 German photograph is an extant anatomical plate, not a 15 ka fossil" ;
